WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:04.557
By late afternoon things were almost settled.

2
00:00:04.558 --> 00:00:07.941
Daisy was at Grace's house with Kaleem.

3
00:00:07.942 --> 00:00:11.521
Beatrice was on her headband.

4
00:00:11.522 --> 00:00:15.621
"I just called Mrs. Ortiz," Grace's mom announced.

5
00:00:15.622 --> 00:00:18.083
"Scamp can stay with us."

6
00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.699
The kids cheered.

7
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.770
"Thanks for the great idea, Daisy," Grace said.

8
00:00:24.771 --> 00:00:29.283
Daisy nodded. Then she whispered to Kaleem.

9
00:00:29.284 --> 00:00:36.388
"Distract Grace for a second. I want to explain things to the fish."

10
00:00:36.389 --> 00:00:43.798
Once they were gone, Daisy stepped over to the fish tank.

11
00:00:43.799 --> 00:00:46.993
"Hi, fish. You're going to be moving."

12
00:00:46.994 --> 00:00:52.461
"To a new tank?" a fish asked, sounding bored.

13
00:00:52.462 --> 00:00:57.760
"No, your whole tank is moving to a new place." Daisy smiled.

14
00:00:57.761 --> 00:01:03.199
"You see, Mrs. Ortiz can't keep Scamp. But she still wants—"

15
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.279
"You talk about humans all the time," another fish said.

16
00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:13.501
"You should talk about us—and admire our beauty."

17
00:01:13.502 --> 00:01:16.888
Daisy giggled. "That's what I'm trying to tell you.

18
00:01:16.889 --> 00:01:20.855
Soon you'll have someone admiring you all day long.

19
00:01:20.856 --> 00:01:24.315
You're moving with Mrs. Ortiz to her son's condo.

20
00:01:24.316 --> 00:01:29.463
She’s not allowed to have a dog there, but fish are just fine."

21
00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:36.632
"Naturally," a fish said. "Fish are the only truly excellent creatures."

22
00:01:36.633 --> 00:01:40.756
Beatrice buzzed in a way that sounded like a snort.

23
00:01:40.757 --> 00:01:43.993
"Fish aren't that great," she muttered.

24
00:01:43.994 --> 00:01:49.438
"Anyway, with your tank gone, Scamp can live here," Daisy said.

25
00:01:49.439 --> 00:01:56.825
"He'll be moving in as soon as you're gone. Now everyone is happy."

26
00:01:56.826 --> 00:02:00.056
Beatrice cheered in Daisy's ear.

27
00:02:00.057 --> 00:02:03.233
"You did it, Daisy! I knew you could—"

28
00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:11.491
Beatrice suddenly felt an odd tug, and then . . . Poof!

29
00:02:11.492 --> 00:02:17.647
The bumblebee found herself back on the rocky beach with the Council of Animals.

30
00:02:17.648 --> 00:02:23.302
Beatrice shook her head.

31
00:02:23.303 --> 00:02:28.419
"Has it already been a week? Is that why I'm back?"

32
00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:30.328
The elephant nodded.

33
00:02:30.329 --> 00:02:35.309
"What news do you have about our young ambassador?"

34
00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:37.196
Beatrice thought for a moment.

35
00:02:37.197 --> 00:02:43.563
"Well, Daisy loves talking with animals. She's helped many already."

36
00:02:43.564 --> 00:02:49.490
Beatrice told the council about Scamp, Floyd, and all of Daisy's other adventures.

37
00:02:49.491 --> 00:02:55.229
"So she's doing well," the pig said. "Have there been any problems?"

38
00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:59.469
Beatrice hesitated. "Perhaps one problem.

39
00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:02.888
She told her best friend about her new ability."

40
00:03:02.889 --> 00:03:05.663
"What?" the magpie cried.

41
00:03:05.664 --> 00:03:07.722
Beatrice buzzed nervously.

42
00:03:07.723 --> 00:03:13.491
"I'm sorry. I think it was my fault for not being clear with her."

43
00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:17.963
"This is a grave problem." The elephant looked upset.

44
00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:22.563
"Were there any other issues we should know about?"

45
00:03:22.564 --> 00:03:26.392
"She almost told a few other people," Beatrice said.

46
00:03:26.393 --> 00:03:28.962
"But she didn't in the end!

47
00:03:28.963 --> 00:03:32.291
And she almost gave up when she couldn't find a home for Scamp.

48
00:03:32.292 --> 00:03:35.552
But then she figured out how to help him."

49
00:03:35.553 --> 00:03:38.486
The council members exchanged looks.

50
00:03:38.487 --> 00:03:42.060
"Hmm," the sea turtle said.

51
00:03:42.061 --> 00:03:48.189
"I suppose we can continue the experiment—at least for now."

52
00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:52.842
"F-for now?" Beatrice said. "What do you mean?"

53
00:03:52.843 --> 00:03:58.752
"If the human ambassador makes too many mistakes, we'll have to remove her gift."

54
00:03:58.753 --> 00:04:00.688
The elephant lifted her trunk.

55
00:04:00.689 --> 00:04:05.278
"We'll bring you back in due time for another report."

56
00:04:05.279 --> 00:04:08.225
"Good luck, little bee," the magpie said.

57
00:04:08.226 --> 00:04:14.132
"We're counting on you and your young human friend.

58
00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:18.398
What's her name again?"

59
00:04:18.399 --> 00:04:23.119
"Daisy," Beatrice said, preparing to be magically transported again.

60
00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:29.930
"Daisy Dolittle."

